==Strategy==
This stage has a ton of enemies with [[Surge Attack]]s, making it very important to bring [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Cats with Surge Immunity]]. [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] is a must-have for its immunity to Surge and its [[Strong Against]] [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku enemies]], but beware of it getting shredded by Mini Angel Cyclone, whom you should be bringing units to constantly knockback as well.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Phantasmal Nobunaga]]: With his Ultra Form, he turns the stage into a cakewalk by permafreezing the Aku enemies and getting extra hits off via Counter-Surge.
*[[Night Oracle Rei (Uber Rare Cat)|Heavenly Herald Rei]]: Making use of her surge immunity and slow, she destroys this stage by both shrugging off its main gimmick and vastly reducing the pushing power of every enemy on this stage, the most threatening one being Mini Angel Cyclone.
*Surge Immune Backliners like [[Lucifer the Fallen (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Lucifer]] and [[Amakusa Shiro (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Amakusa]] are especially useful for this stage, given that they can ignore Medu-san's main gimmick entirely.
*[[Talents|Ultra Talented]] [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Akuma Hayabusa]]: After his Surge Immunity Ultra Talent is unlocked, Hayabusa can be a massive help on this stage. With Strong Against, Slow and Knockback against Aku enemies, he can destroy them with just a few attacks. The only enemy to look out for is Mini Angel Cyclone, as if can push into his blindspot if unchecked.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]]: With its Surge immunity talent, Diabolosa is a hard-counter to this stage with it dealing Massive damage to everything in the stage and its decently fast attack rate it can shred everything here. If you have an extra slot, you can pair it with [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Flying Cat]] for the [[Land-Air Assault (Combo)|Land-Air Assault]] combo for a 15% attack boost for your whole team.
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]]: Lasvoss outranges everything here and deals HUGE damage with a savage blow and still does good damage without it. Also, the [[Bad Guys (Combo)|Bad Guys]] combo can be a big help for units like [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]].
*[[Bunny & Canard (Uber Rare Cat)|Malevolent Mad-Duck]]: Due to outranging all enemies in this stage and having surge immunity, they are a good choice for this stage. Just bring something to deal with the Mini Angel Cyclones, as they are unable to attack them.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]]: Any form works here. Thunder Jack's colossal 18,000 DPS and a quite tanky 119,000 HP (at level 30) shreds through most to all of the Mini Angel Cyclone's KBs, and deals notable supplemental damage to the Aku enemies as well. You do have to provide him enough support, otherwise he may fall early.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Death’s Daughter Lunacia]]: Her Weaken and Strong against Angel and Aku makes her perfect for this stage. Additionally, like Oda, she also has Counter-Surge, which is extremely effective due to the spam of surges.

==Trivia==
*Pursuit of Understanding's Japanese name,  Kai o Motomete Sanzenri (解を求めて三千里, "3000 Leagues in Search of the Solution"), is a reference to the anime ''[[wikipedia:3000 Leagues in Search of Mother|3000 Leagues in Search of Mother]]''.
*Like [[1 + 2 = Tor]] and [[Isosceles Valley]], Pursuit of Understanding appears to have been designed specifically for one of the [[Ultra Form]]s added in [[Version 13.0 Update|Version 13.0]] alongside [[Demon of Deciliter Bay]]. In this case, Pursuit of Understanding's [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] and [[Surge Attack]]s make it ideal for testing [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Phantasmal Nobunaga]]'s Aku target and Counter-Surge ability.

